# fixedbugs, 2026-09-08 (defect 020, found by panel 120's compiler-engineer
# while enumerating the embedded library to answer whether the spec's list of
# built-ins is complete).
#
# SYMPTOM: `print(HERO_OS_OK)` ran and printed `0` from a plain user program.
# Four names the program never declared were in its scope, and reading one
# meant relying on the compiler's own plumbing.
#
# CAUSE: panel 033 R5 walled off the library's extern FUNCTIONS —
# `function filter` is `builtin_name_taken`, `hero_args_count()` is
# `extern_across_modules` — and `selfhost/resolve/names.hero` grouped
# `.constant_decl` with `.record_decl` and `.test_decl` in one arm with no
# `is_extern` guard, where `.function_decl` carried one twice. The grouped arm
# could not ask the question, which is why it was wrong: it rested on a premise
# about the world, that a constant cannot be extern, and the library declares
# four that are.
#
# FIX: the arm splits and asks the declaration in hand. A constant is extern
# exactly when it has a HEADER where an ordinary one has a body, and a record
# the same, so `record_decl` is guarded too — WITH NO WITNESS TODAY, because
# the library declares no records. The class is closed rather than the case
# that happened to be reachable (`.claude/rules/module-shape.md`: a narrowing
# asks the value, never the world).
#
# The message lost the word "callable" in the same commit and gained
# "reachable", which the neighbouring module doc had used all along: a
# constant is read rather than called, and before this repair no constant ever
# reached that sentence.

function main()
    print(HERO_OS_OK)  #~ extern_across_modules
    print(HERO_OS_NOT_FOUND)  #~ extern_across_modules
    print(HERO_STR_OK)  #~ extern_across_modules
